   "text": "1. Corruption charged as a reason to act: Hawaii, 1892–93, and Korea, 1894",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "These four documents show corruption being alleged, by an American minister and by a foreign government, as the ground for action against a third country's rulers. They matter because the allegation did the work of an argument, and because the printed record itself contains the counter-charge. Whether Washington acted because of the charge is not shown by them."
  },
